      sources: "Sources: Chapter 02, “Checklist”; workbook index, Chapter 03; Learn, Microsoft Graph national cloud deployments.",
      say: `Here's what done looks like. On the cloud side: an explicit cloud name that fails on anything unknown, no government hosts in the GCC configuration, the right authority and scope for every credential, one token per resource, and the token never leaving the cloud's Graph host. On the run side: every call declared with its least privileged permission, an app that holds exactly those, paging and retries done Microsoft's way, and beta declared and labeled. Next, Chapter 3 uses these rules to write a validation kit check. Thanks for watching.`,
      detail: `Checklist: the client takes an explicit cloud name and raises on any name it doesn't know. GCC uses login.microsoftonline.com, graph.microsoft.com and, for Azure, management.azure.com; nothing in the GCC configuration is a .us host. Every credential names the cloud's authority (or is a managed identity), and every scope names the cloud's host. One token per resource: Graph and Resource Manager are never asked for in one request. No URL, including a nextLink, is sent to a host other than the cloud's Graph host. Every call is in graph-calls.json with its least-privileged permission, and the task's permission list is the union of its calls. The app registration holds exactly the task's permissions, with a certificate or managed identity, never a secret. Paging sends the same headers on every page and retries with the last good link. Throttling waits for Retry-After, backs off when it's missing, and stops after a limit. Every beta call is declared, read through try_beta or Get-FmwBetaCollection, and labeled in the output. The pinned Microsoft snippets match their manifest, and every upstream commit since the pin has been reviewed. Next: Chapter 03 — Writing a Validation Kit Check: a new check, VK-SYNC-02, from the catalog entry through pass and fail fixtures and Pester tests to the GET-only safety rule, and what to do when the read needs a privileged role.`,
